Z||000000||overlord||07-05-2001||04:39 PM||||once and a while ill be driving along and the check engine light will come on for maybe 10-20 secs then shut off.  I'm not sure but it also seems to shut off when i put the tranny into neutral (coincidence)?<P>It doesnt do it all the time....just seems like a random thing.  Coolant is good and temperature is good,  oil level is good.<BR>84 duke.<P>I'm guessing its just the light....but maybe someone else has seen this and might know if there is actually something wrong.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Wolfhound||07-05-2001||05:14 PM||||Have you checked for set codes?||||reg||1
Z||000002||johnt671||07-05-2001||05:21 PM||||You reed to go into the ecand get the code so you can find out what is causing the light to come on.  You should get a manual for the car so you can look up the codes and fix the problem before it gets worse.  If you get the book(I have both haynes and chilton) the tell you how to get into the computer and read the codes. Its easy to do.  If you don't have the book all you do is remove the cover around the cigarette lighter and you will see a terminal over near the pass side,  Use a paper clip or a small piece of wire and jump the two tenminals on the lower right side together and turn the ign. to on.  Don't start the car.  The check engine light will flash once pause and flash twice for a code 12.  This will happen three times.  Then the light will flash again to give you the trouble codes.  Write them down and when the check is done the light will again flash three times and you will have the reasons why your light comes on.  after you repair the problem disconnect your battery for ten seconds and you will erase the stored codes.  Look them up in the book or post them here and someone can let you know what they mean||||reg||1
